            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0748" n="666" xml:id="pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-22T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1925—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Since the President informed me this morning that he has no objection, the
                    American troops will be withdrawn from the city tomorrow.</p>
                <p>The Government has brought many police from the interior, increasing the forces
                    in the city from about 250 to about 400 men. The President tells me that this
                    increase will be temporary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
